-- =====================================================================
-- Session 496 migration — canon / Mark 1–16 — Phase 2 REBUILD, batch m1: the orphan cards rewritten Come-and-See and threaded.
-- 169 cards rewritten in place (ids and verse pairs kept), 4 new thread(s), 0 unanchored thread(s) anchored, 169 thread members added.
-- Drafted on: Claude Sonnet 5.5, Claude Sonnet 5.5 (claude-sonnet-5-5), claude-fable-5-1 (Fable 5.1), claude-sonnet-5-5, claude-sonnet-5-5 (Sonnet 5.5); read and corrected on Claude Fable 5.1; every note composed by script (assemble496.py): target verse whole
-- from parsed/canon.json (restored-names KJV, the canon convention), Mark verse whole from the live text of the read-back, then the prose.
-- Safety (DO block, before any write): RAISES if a card id is gone or sits on another verse pair, if a Mark verse's live text differs from the
-- read-back, if a card's live note is neither the note this was written against nor the new one, if a card is already in a thread this file does
-- not put it in, if a thread to join / an anchor verse is missing, or if a thread to anchor already has a different anchor.
-- Idempotent: a re-run reports 0 rewritten / 0 inserted / 0 anchored.  Nothing is deleted.
-- Run: python3 api/apply_migration.py data-schema/migrations/session496_mark_m1_rebuild.sql
-- =====================================================================
\echo 'session496 — Mark 1–16 rebuild starting...'
BEGIN;
CREATE TEMP TABLE _s496_m1_c (id BIGINT, src_ch INT, src_v INT, src_text TEXT, tgt_slug TEXT, tgt_ch INT, tgt_v INT, old_note TEXT, new_note TEXT) ON COMMIT DROP;
CREATE TEMP TABLE _s496_m1_t (slug TEXT, title TEXT, summary_md TEXT, ch INT, a_vn INT, z_vn INT, tier TEXT, sort_order INT) ON COMMIT DROP;

*And as they came down from the mountain, he charged them that they should tell no man what things they had seen, till the Son of Adam were risen from the dead.* (Mark 9:9)

What lies between the glory and the rising had been written already, in the picture of a man the people would not own.

*He is despised and rejected of men; a man of sorrows, and acquainted with grief: and we hid as it were our faces from him; he was despised, and we esteemed him not.* (Isaiah 53:3)

Then, passing through Galilee, he stops hinting and teaches the twelve plainly.

*For he taught his disciples, and said unto them, The Son of Adam is delivered into the hands of men, and they shall kill him; and after that he is killed, he shall rise the third day.* (Mark 9:31)

Isaiah has the same road, and says whose transgression stands behind it.

*He was taken from prison and from judgment: and who shall declare his generation? for he was cut off out of the land of the living: for the transgression of my people was he stricken.* (Isaiah 53:8)

Zechariah has the flock's side of it, the shepherd smitten by the sword Yahuah (the LORD) of hosts calls up, and the sheep scattering after.

*Awake, O sword, against my shepherd, and against the man that is my fellow, saith Yahuah Tseva'ot (LORD of hosts): smite the shepherd, and the sheep shall be scattered: and I will turn mine hand upon the little ones.* (Zechariah 13:7)

So when Mark says the twelve *understood not that saying*, the fault was not that the saying was new. The despised man, the one taken from judgment and cut off from the living, and the shepherd with the scattering flock were already on the page they had been reading all their lives.$n$,9,9,32,'free',13244),
('mark-12-more-than-all-whole-burnt-offerings-the-scribe-says-what-the-prophets-said',$n$More than all whole burnt offerings — the scribe says what the prophets said$n$,$n$It ain't new. A scribe asks which commandment is first, hears the answer, and agrees. Then he goes a step further.

*And to love him with all the heart, and with all the understanding, and with all the soul, and with all the strength, and to love his neighbour as himself, is more than all whole burnt offerings and sacrifices.* (Mark 12:33)

Yahusha (Jesus) says he answered discreetly, and the prophets show why. Hosea had put it in the voice of Yahuah (the LORD) himself.

*For I desired mercy, and not sacrifice; and the knowledge of Elohim (God) more than burnt offerings.* (Hosea 6:6)

Samuel had said it to a king who thought an offering could stand in for hearing.

*And Samuel said, Hath Yahuah (LORD) as great delight in burnt offerings and sacrifices, as in obeying the voice of Yahuah (LORD)? Behold, to obey is better than sacrifice, and to hearken than the fat of rams.* (1 Samuel 15:22)

And Micah asks the worshipper's question, how much he must bring.

*Wherewith shall I come before Yahuah (LORD), and bow myself before the high Elohim (God)? shall I come before him with burnt offerings, with calves of a year old?* (Micah 6:6)

The answer comes a few verses on.

*He hath shewed thee, O man, what is good; and what doth Yahuah (LORD) require of thee, but to do justly, and to love mercy, and to walk humbly with thy Elohim (God)?* (Micah 6:8)

The scribe is not setting the offerings aside, and neither did these three. Each puts the commandment's heart, hearing the voice, mercy, love of Elohim (God) and the neighbour, above the gift laid on the altar, and the scribe says it back to Yahusha (Jesus) in their words.$n$,12,28,34,'free',3264),
('mark-13-signs-and-wonders-do-not-vouch-for-the-prophet',$n$Signs and wonders do not vouch for the prophet$n$,$n$It ain't new. Yahusha (Jesus) warns the four who asked him privately on the Mount of Olives that the deceivers will not come empty-handed:

*For false Christs and false prophets shall rise, and shall shew signs and wonders, to seduce, if it were possible, even the elect.* (Mark 13:22)

Moses had already told Yashar'el (Israel) that a sign proves nothing by being a sign. What matters is where the man who gives it is leading:

*If there arise among you a prophet, or a dreamer of dreams, and giveth thee a sign or a wonder,* (Deuteronomy 13:1)

*And the sign or the wonder come to pass, whereof he spake unto thee, saying, Let us go after other gods, which thou hast not known, and let us serve them;* (Deuteronomy 13:2)

The answer Moses gives is the commandments themselves:

*Ye shall walk after Yahuah Elohaychem (the LORD your God), and fear him, and keep his commandments, and obey his voice, and ye shall serve him, and cleave unto him.* (Deuteronomy 13:4)

So a wonder that comes to pass is no proof. The test is whether the one who works it keeps the people walking in the commandments or draws them away.

John saw wonders of this kind in Revelation, in his own vision:

*And he doeth great wonders, so that he maketh fire come down from heaven on the earth in the sight of men,* (Revelation 13:13)

And Paul, writing to the Thessalonians, says where such power comes from:

*Even him, whose coming is after the working of Satan with all power and signs and lying wonders,* (2 Thessalonians 2:9)

Moses, John and Paul agree with what Yahusha (Jesus) says in Mark: signs and wonders can be seen, and they can still seduce.$n$,13,22,22,'free',1251),
('mark-13-the-son-of-adam-coming-in-the-clouds',$n$The Son of Adam coming in the clouds$n$,$n$Yahusha (Jesus) answers the four who asked him privately by naming himself as the one Daniel saw:

*And then shall they see the Son of Adam coming in the clouds with great power and glory.* (Mark 13:26)

Daniel saw him in a night vision, and what he saw was one like the Son of Adam:

*I saw in the night visions, and, behold, one like the Son of Adam came with the clouds of heaven, and came to the Ancient of days, and they brought him near before him.* (Daniel 7:13)

Daniel goes on to say what was given him:

*And there was given him dominion, and glory, and a kingdom, that all people, nations, and languages, should serve him: his dominion is an everlasting dominion, which shall not pass away, and his kingdom that which shall not be destroyed.* (Daniel 7:14)

Matthew tells the same coming and adds the mourning of the tribes:

*And then shall appear the sign of the Son of Adam in heaven: and then shall all the tribes of the earth mourn, and they shall see the Son of Adam coming in the clouds of heaven with power and great glory.* (Matthew 24:30)

John, in Revelation, says every eye will see him:

*Behold, he cometh with clouds; and every eye shall see him, and they also which pierced him: and all kindreds of the earth shall wail because of him. Even so, Amen.* (Revelation 1:7)

And Zechariah, long before, has the speaker say of the pierced one:

*And I will pour upon the house of David, and upon the inhabitants of Jerusalem, the spirit of grace and of supplications: and they shall look upon me whom they have pierced, and they shall mourn for him, as one mourneth for his only son, and shall be in bitterness for him, as one that is in bitterness for his firstborn.* (Zechariah 12:10)

The one Daniel saw and the one Mark names are one, and the seeing ends in mourning for the one who was pierced.$n$,13,26,26,'free',1252);
CREATE TEMP TABLE _s496_m1_a (slug TEXT, book TEXT, ch INT, a_vn INT, z_vn INT) ON COMMIT DROP;
-- (no rows for _s496_m1_a)
CREATE TEMP TABLE _s496_m1_m (thread_slug TEXT, card_id BIGINT, ord INT, member_note TEXT) ON COMMIT DROP;

CREATE OR REPLACE TEMP VIEW _s496_m1_lookup AS
SELECT b.slug AS book_slug, c.chapter_number, v.verse_number, v.id AS verse_id, v.text
  FROM verses v JOIN chapters c ON v.chapter_id = c.id JOIN books b ON c.book_id = b.id
  JOIN editions e ON b.edition_id = e.id
 WHERE e.slug = 'canon';

DO $s496$
DECLARE r RECORD; sid BIGINT; tid BIGINT; ltext TEXT; cur RECORD; n INT; av BIGINT; zv BIGINT;
        n_note INT := 0; n_note_same INT := 0; n_thr INT := 0; n_thr_same INT := 0; n_anc INT := 0; n_anc_same INT := 0; n_mem INT := 0; n_mem_same INT := 0; n_total INT;
BEGIN
  -- ---- guards: every row is checked before anything is written ----
  FOR r IN SELECT * FROM _s496_m1_c LOOP
    SELECT verse_id, text INTO sid, ltext FROM _s496_m1_lookup WHERE book_slug = 'mark' AND chapter_number = r.src_ch AND verse_number = r.src_v;
    IF sid IS NULL THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'S496: source verse mark %:% missing', r.src_ch, r.src_v; END IF;
    IF ltext <> r.src_text THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'S496: live text of mark %:% differs from the read-back this migration was written against — re-run the dump and rebuild', r.src_ch, r.src_v; END IF;
    SELECT verse_id INTO tid FROM _s496_m1_lookup WHERE book_slug = r.tgt_slug AND chapter_number = r.tgt_ch AND verse_number = r.tgt_v;
    IF tid IS NULL THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'S496: target verse % %:% missing', r.tgt_slug, r.tgt_ch, r.tgt_v; END IF;
    SELECT * INTO cur FROM cross_references WHERE id = r.id;
    IF NOT FOUND THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'S496: card % is gone', r.id; END IF;
    IF cur.source_verse_id <> sid OR cur.target_verse_id <> tid THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'S496: card % no longer sits on mark %:% -> % %:%', r.id, r.src_ch, r.src_v, r.tgt_slug, r.tgt_ch, r.tgt_v; END IF;
    IF cur.note IS DISTINCT FROM r.old_note AND cur.note IS DISTINCT FROM r.new_note THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'S496: the live note of card % differs from the read-back this migration was written against — re-run the dump and rebuild', r.id; END IF;
    IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cross_reference_thread_members mm JOIN cross_reference_threads th ON th.id = mm.thread_id
                WHERE mm.cross_reference_id = r.id AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM _s496_m1_m m WHERE m.card_id = r.id AND m.thread_slug = th.slug)) THEN
      RAISE EXCEPTION 'S496: card % already sits in a thread this migration does not put it in — re-run the dump and rebuild', r.id; END IF;
  END LOOP;
  FOR r IN SELECT * FROM _s496_m1_t LOOP
    IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM _s496_m1_lookup WHERE book_slug = 'mark' AND chapter_number = r.ch AND verse_number = r.a_vn)
    OR NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM _s496_m1_lookup WHERE book_slug = 'mark' AND chapter_number = r.ch AND verse_number = r.z_vn) THEN
      RAISE EXCEPTION 'S496: anchor %:%-% for new thread % missing', r.ch, r.a_vn, r.z_vn, r.slug; END IF;
  END LOOP;
  FOR r IN SELECT * FROM _s496_m1_a LOOP
    SELECT verse_id INTO av FROM _s496_m1_lookup WHERE book_slug = r.book AND chapter_number = r.ch AND verse_number = r.a_vn;
    SELECT verse_id INTO zv FROM _s496_m1_lookup WHERE book_slug = r.book AND chapter_number = r.ch AND verse_number = r.z_vn;
    IF av IS NULL OR zv IS NULL THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'S496: anchor verse % %:%-% for thread % missing', r.book, r.ch, r.a_vn, r.z_vn, r.slug; END IF;
    SELECT * INTO cur FROM cross_reference_threads WHERE slug = r.slug;
    IF NOT FOUND THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'S496: thread to anchor % does not exist', r.slug; END IF;
    IF cur.anchor_verse_id_start IS NOT NULL AND (cur.anchor_verse_id_start <> av OR cur.anchor_verse_id_end IS DISTINCT FROM zv) THEN
      RAISE EXCEPTION 'S496: thread % already carries a different anchor — re-run the dump and rebuild', r.slug; END IF;
  END LOOP;
  FOR r IN SELECT DISTINCT thread_slug FROM _s496_m1_m LOOP
    IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cross_reference_threads WHERE slug = r.thread_slug) AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM _s496_m1_t WHERE slug = r.thread_slug) THEN
      RAISE EXCEPTION 'S496: thread to join % does not exist', r.thread_slug; END IF;
  END LOOP;

  -- ---- notes rewritten in place ----
  SELECT count(*) INTO n_total FROM _s496_m1_c;
  UPDATE cross_references x SET note = c.new_note FROM _s496_m1_c c WHERE x.id = c.id AND x.note IS DISTINCT FROM c.new_note;
  GET DIAGNOSTICS n_note = ROW_COUNT; n_note_same := n_total - n_note;

  -- ---- new threads ----
  SELECT count(*) INTO n_total FROM _s496_m1_t;
  SELECT t.slug, t.title, t.summary_md, sv.verse_id, ev.verse_id, t.tier::content_tier, t.sort_order
    FROM _s496_m1_t t
    JOIN _s496_m1_lookup sv ON sv.book_slug='mark' AND sv.chapter_number=t.ch AND sv.verse_number=t.a_vn
    JOIN _s496_m1_lookup ev ON ev.book_slug='mark' AND ev.chapter_number=t.ch AND ev.verse_number=t.z_vn
  ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;
  GET DIAGNOSTICS n_thr = ROW_COUNT; n_thr_same := n_total - n_thr;

  -- ---- anchors for the unanchored threads these cards join ----
  SELECT count(*) INTO n_total FROM _s496_m1_a;
  UPDATE cross_reference_threads th SET anchor_verse_id_start = sv.verse_id, anchor_verse_id_end = ev.verse_id
    FROM _s496_m1_a a
    JOIN _s496_m1_lookup sv ON sv.book_slug=a.book AND sv.chapter_number=a.ch AND sv.verse_number=a.a_vn
    JOIN _s496_m1_lookup ev ON ev.book_slug=a.book AND ev.chapter_number=a.ch AND ev.verse_number=a.z_vn
   WHERE th.slug = a.slug AND th.anchor_verse_id_start IS NULL;
  GET DIAGNOSTICS n_anc = ROW_COUNT; n_anc_same := n_total - n_anc;

  -- ---- members: each card into its thread, after the thread's live maximum, in source verse order ----
  SELECT count(*) INTO n_total FROM _s496_m1_m;
  SELECT th.id, m.card_id,
         COALESCE((SELECT max(mm.sort_order) FROM cross_reference_thread_members mm WHERE mm.thread_id = th.id), 0)
           + row_number() OVER (PARTITION BY th.id ORDER BY m.ord, m.card_id),
         m.member_note
    FROM _s496_m1_m m JOIN cross_reference_threads th ON th.slug = m.thread_slug
   WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cross_reference_thread_members mm WHERE mm.thread_id = th.id AND mm.cross_reference_id = m.card_id)
  ON CONFLICT (thread_id, cross_reference_id) DO NOTHING;
  GET DIAGNOSTICS n_mem = ROW_COUNT; n_mem_same := n_total - n_mem;

  -- ---- proof before commit: every card carries its new note and sits in its thread ----
  SELECT count(*) INTO n FROM _s496_m1_c c JOIN cross_references x ON x.id = c.id WHERE x.note IS DISTINCT FROM c.new_note;
  IF n > 0 THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'S496: % card(s) do not carry the new note', n; END IF;
  SELECT count(*) INTO n FROM _s496_m1_m m WHERE NOT EXISTS (
    SELECT 1 FROM cross_reference_thread_members mm JOIN cross_reference_threads th ON th.id = mm.thread_id AND th.slug = m.thread_slug WHERE mm.cross_reference_id = m.card_id);
  IF n > 0 THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'S496: % member row(s) did not land', n; END IF;
  SELECT count(*) INTO n FROM _s496_m1_a a JOIN cross_reference_threads th ON th.slug = a.slug WHERE th.anchor_verse_id_start IS NULL;
  IF n > 0 THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'S496: % thread(s) still unanchored', n; END IF;

  RAISE NOTICE 'S496 (mark m1) summary: notes rewritten % / already there %; threads inserted % / already there %; anchors set % / already there %; members inserted % / already there %',
    n_note, n_note_same, n_thr, n_thr_same, n_anc, n_anc_same, n_mem, n_mem_same;
END $s496$;
COMMIT;
\echo 'session496 — Mark 1–16 rebuild done.'
